<newsitem itemid="42148" id="root" date="1996-09-09" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Hammerson says H1 net rental income up.</title>
<headline>Hammerson says H1 net rental income up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		8.2		    vs 7.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.7		    vs 3.5</p>
<p> Pretax profit *	  31.2		   vs 32.1</p>
<p> Net rental income	63.3		   vs 62.9</p>
<p>NOTE - * UK property group Hammerson Plc said profit before taxation for the first six months of 1996 was 31.2 million stg excluding exceptional profits arising from the sale of investment properties of 0.9 million stg. It said there was an improvement of 2.0 million stg in net rental income in the UK.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 57.0		   vs 56.4</p>
<p> Net taxed		  25.2		   vs 23.1</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 13</p>
<p>Div  registration date September 9  Ex-div date		September 16</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
